ey from the family Falconidae endemic to the forests of Mauritius, where it is restricted to the southwestern plateau's forests, cliffs, and ravines."},{"id":"3DTGN","name":"Falco rufigularis","rank":"species","names":3,"auth":"Daudin, 1800","common":"Bat Falcon","kids":3,"wiki":"Bat falcon","img":{"url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/OFalco%20rufigularis%20Bat%20Falcon.jpg?width=320","license":"CC BY 2.0","author":"Joao Quental","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:OFalco%20rufigularis%20Bat%20Falcon.jpg"},"descSrc":"wikipedia","desc":"The bat falcon (Falco rufigularis) is a bird of prey in the family Falconidae, the falcons and caracaras."},{"id":"3DTGP","name":"Falco rupicoloides","rank":"species","names":3,"auth":"A. Smith, 1829","common":"Greater Kestrel","kids":3,"wiki":"Greater kestrel","img":{"url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Greater%20Kestrel%20Namibia.jpg?width=320","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","author":"Thomas Schoch","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greater%20Kestrel%20Namibia.jpg"},"descSrc":"wikipedia","desc":"The greater kestrel (Falco rupicoloides) or white-eyed kestrel is a bird of prey belonging to the falcon family Falconidae."},{"id":"3DTGQ","name":"Falco rupicolus","rank":"species","names":0,"auth":"Daudin, 1800","common":"Rock Kestrel","wiki":"Rock kestrel","img":{"url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Rock%20Kestrel%20%28Falco%20rupicolus%29%2C%20Mountain%20Zebra%20NP%2C%20South%20Africa.jpg?width=320","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","author":"Bernard DUPONT from FRANCE","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rock%20Kestrel%20%28Falco%20rupicolus%29%2C%20Mountain%20Zebra%20NP%2C%20South%20Africa.jpg"},"descSrc":"wikipedia","desc":"The rock kestrel (Falco rupicolus) is a bird of prey species belonging to the kestrel group of the falcon family Falconidae."},{"id":"3DTGR","name":"Falco rusticolus","rank":"species","names":0,"auth":"Linnaeus, 1758","common":